1
00:00:01,721 --> 00:00:03,180
[opening theme music playing]

2
00:01:31,018 --> 00:01:35,981
SWEET HUNGER

3
00:01:40,361 --> 00:01:43,072
"I can see that you're big and strong."

4
00:01:43,155 --> 00:01:45,574
"But you wouldn't eat me, would you?"

5
00:01:48,244 --> 00:01:49,787
Is that too high and mighty?

6
00:01:51,330 --> 00:01:53,499
"I can see that you're big and strong...

7
00:01:53,582 --> 00:01:56,627
but... you wouldn't eat me, would you?"

8
00:01:57,128 --> 00:02:00,131
Just terrible! Now I sound too scared.

9
00:02:00,214 --> 00:02:03,634
This girl is supposed to trust
her carnivore friend, not fear them.

10
00:02:04,510 --> 00:02:08,180
But wait, does trust have
a different sound than friendship?

11
00:02:08,722 --> 00:02:09,974
How about...

12
00:02:10,057 --> 00:02:13,102
"Hang on, you wouldn't eat me, would you?"

13
00:02:13,769 --> 00:02:15,938
[groans] Still wrong!

14
00:02:17,148 --> 00:02:18,149
[sighs]

15
00:02:20,860 --> 00:02:25,781
I WANT TO ASK YOU SOMETHING,
CAN WE MEET THIS AFTERNOON?

16
00:02:26,282 --> 00:02:28,492
[Juno]
"I can see that you're big and strong,

17
00:02:29,535 --> 00:02:31,620
but you wouldn't eat me, would you?"

18
00:02:32,246 --> 00:02:33,622
Oh...

19
00:02:34,123 --> 00:02:36,792
- "But... you wouldn't eat me, would you?"
- What the...

20
00:02:37,376 --> 00:02:39,753
{\an8}- What are you doing, Juno?
- [Juno] What?

21
00:02:40,421 --> 00:02:42,798
Oh! No, this is, uh, for drama club.

22
00:02:42,882 --> 00:02:44,884
[Lemur] I'm glad you were just acting.

23
00:02:44,967 --> 00:02:46,468
You don't want to overdo it.

24
00:02:46,552 --> 00:02:48,721
Juno's always worrying
about something.

25
00:02:48,804 --> 00:02:51,140
- Oh, you've put on some weight.
- Really? No!

26
00:02:51,223 --> 00:02:53,267
I guess you eat
when you're stressed out?

27
00:02:53,350 --> 00:02:55,686
[laughs] Well, I say eat up.

28
00:02:55,769 --> 00:02:58,814
Do what you want.
You're a senior, not a freshman.

29
00:02:58,898 --> 00:03:00,691
- You heard the news?
- What?

30
00:03:00,774 --> 00:03:04,570
I felt like something big was coming,
but I didn't expect this.

31
00:03:04,653 --> 00:03:07,448
Well, he's a Beastar candidate,
so why not?

32
00:03:07,531 --> 00:03:09,867
Uh, hold on. What are you talking about?

33
00:03:09,950 --> 00:03:11,660
What? You don't know?

34
00:03:12,953 --> 00:03:13,996
Take a look.

35
00:03:14,079 --> 00:03:15,456
MAYOR, ZOOLYMPIC BID...
"LOUIS APPOINTED AS AMBASSADOR"

36
00:03:15,539 --> 00:03:19,627
- They named him Zoolympic Ambassador!
- That makes him a celebrity now, right?

37
00:03:19,710 --> 00:03:22,421
Well, was he ever really "normal"
like the rest of us?

38
00:03:22,504 --> 00:03:24,381
I know what you mean.

39
00:03:25,007 --> 00:03:26,008
[chuckles nervously]

40
00:03:26,592 --> 00:03:29,053
<i>Okay. I just need to calm down.</i>

41
00:03:29,136 --> 00:03:31,347
<i>He's going to still have time for me.</i>

42
00:03:31,430 --> 00:03:33,557
<i>Right? Yeah, I'm sure.</i>

43
00:03:33,641 --> 00:03:35,267
- [phone beeps]
- Huh?

44
00:03:37,937 --> 00:03:40,147
[frustrated sigh]

45
00:03:42,983 --> 00:03:46,528
Sorry for the wait, guys.
Let me know if you need anything else.

46
00:03:47,488 --> 00:03:48,489
Oh.

47
00:03:50,908 --> 00:03:51,867
Hey...

48
00:03:52,534 --> 00:03:55,120
Roar! Do you like my lion?

49
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:57,289
[laughs]

50
00:03:58,457 --> 00:04:00,292
- [Haru] Here you go.
- Thank you!

51
00:04:00,376 --> 00:04:02,503
[mother] That was sweet of you
to bring that back.

52
00:04:02,586 --> 00:04:04,546
- [Haru] Do you like lions?
- Mm-hm!

53
00:04:04,630 --> 00:04:06,590
I'm going to be a lion when I grow up.

54
00:04:07,132 --> 00:04:08,801
- Is that so? A lion?
- [donkey foal laughs]

55
00:04:08,884 --> 00:04:10,010
Because they're cute!

56
00:04:11,929 --> 00:04:13,847
- [shop clerk] Hey, Haru!
- Huh?

57
00:04:13,931 --> 00:04:16,350
{\an8}- Service table six.
- [Haru] Yeah, on it.

58
00:04:19,520 --> 00:04:21,313
- Careful with this.
- Right.

59
00:04:22,273 --> 00:04:23,399
[grunts softly]

60
00:04:33,701 --> 00:04:35,411
I have your order right he-- Whoa!

61
00:04:38,539 --> 00:04:39,540
Juno?

62
00:04:39,623 --> 00:04:40,916
Oh, Haru!

63
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:42,126
[chuckles nervously]

64
00:04:42,209 --> 00:04:43,043
Wha...

65
00:04:43,877 --> 00:04:45,671
{\an8}Uh, did you eat all of those?

66
00:04:45,754 --> 00:04:47,381
Huh? No, of course not!

67
00:04:48,382 --> 00:04:50,134
All right, I did!

68
00:04:50,217 --> 00:04:52,011
[frustrated sigh]

69
00:04:52,678 --> 00:04:53,846
Are you okay?

70
00:04:54,430 --> 00:04:58,225
How about I...
just make some room on the table here.

71
00:04:58,309 --> 00:04:59,935
- [Juno exclaims nervously]
- Huh?

72
00:05:00,561 --> 00:05:03,480
{\an8}Haru, I need a friend right now.

73
00:05:08,652 --> 00:05:12,865
So you're saying, this guy you like,
he has a fiancée?

74
00:05:12,948 --> 00:05:14,450
Unfortunately.

75
00:05:14,533 --> 00:05:16,243
Well, what else can you tell me about him?

76
00:05:16,785 --> 00:05:18,912
He was a senior at my school.

77
00:05:18,996 --> 00:05:21,415
I really wanted to tell him
about my performance.

78
00:05:21,498 --> 00:05:23,667
Oh, he's in the theatre?

79
00:05:23,751 --> 00:05:27,338
He graduated back in the spring,
so he's not around anymore.

80
00:05:27,421 --> 00:05:28,881
You don't see him much?

81
00:05:28,964 --> 00:05:33,260
I mustered up the courage to contact him,
but then this!

82
00:05:33,343 --> 00:05:34,720
What kind of message is that?

83
00:05:34,803 --> 00:05:35,679
I HAVE PLANS WITH MY FIANCÉE TODAY. SORRY.

84
00:05:35,763 --> 00:05:37,056
Look at what he wrote me!

85
00:05:37,139 --> 00:05:37,973
[Haru] <i>It's Louis?</i>

86
00:05:38,057 --> 00:05:39,933
[Juno] Does it get any ruder?

87
00:05:40,434 --> 00:05:43,270
Uhh... You're right, that's pretty cold.

88
00:05:43,353 --> 00:05:44,605
That's what I'm saying!

89
00:05:44,688 --> 00:05:47,066
Who gets someone's hopes up
just to let them down?

90
00:05:47,733 --> 00:05:51,278
[Haru] <i>What's gotten into him?
If this were me, I could handle it.</i>

91
00:05:51,361 --> 00:05:54,615
<i>But Juno's fur isn't thick enough
for these games.</i>

92
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:56,116
<i>Wait a minute.</i>

93
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:58,327
<i>Why do she and I
have the same taste in boys?</i>

94
00:05:58,410 --> 00:06:01,747
Ah, I wonder if he was dating
someone else at school.

95
00:06:01,830 --> 00:06:05,084
Huh? Oh, uh-- That'd be silly.

96
00:06:06,126 --> 00:06:10,798
Well, uh, probably not.
If he's engaged, that'd be weird.

97
00:06:10,881 --> 00:06:15,594
Hm. Arranged relationships
seem so cold to me.

98
00:06:15,677 --> 00:06:17,805
{\an8}You're not allowed to just fall in love.

99
00:06:20,140 --> 00:06:22,768
{\an8}What made you fall for him?
Do you remember?

100
00:06:23,519 --> 00:06:24,353
{\an8}[chuckles]

101
00:06:24,978 --> 00:06:28,023
{\an8}In public, he's always so put together.

102
00:06:28,107 --> 00:06:29,817
{\an8}But in reality...

103
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:33,821
{\an8}[Haru] <i>He puts up a front,
but he can be very vulnerable.</i>

104
00:06:34,530 --> 00:06:36,532
{\an8}<i>That drew me to him, too.</i>

105
00:06:36,615 --> 00:06:39,243
{\an8}He's so cute when he's vulnerable!

106
00:06:39,326 --> 00:06:40,244
Huh?

107
00:06:40,327 --> 00:06:42,913
If you boss him around a little,
he acts put out,

108
00:06:42,996 --> 00:06:44,706
but I can tell he likes it.

109
00:06:44,790 --> 00:06:46,041
- Also--
- Are you serious?

110
00:06:46,125 --> 00:06:48,794
- I mean, is he really like that?
- Oh, yeah.

111
00:06:48,877 --> 00:06:51,130
He's all stoic and intellectual,

112
00:06:51,213 --> 00:06:54,091
but then he's flustered
just like a little kid.

113
00:06:54,174 --> 00:06:56,051
- [chuckles]
- Wow. Imagine that.

114
00:06:56,135 --> 00:07:00,264
I know, it's crazy!
I've never met anyone like that before.

115
00:07:00,806 --> 00:07:04,726
I mean something to him.
Or at least that's what my heart tells me.

116
00:07:05,936 --> 00:07:07,438
But what do I know?

117
00:07:07,521 --> 00:07:08,605
[Haru] Oh, come on.

118
00:07:10,524 --> 00:07:13,444
Haru, what if he's scared
I might try to eat him

119
00:07:13,527 --> 00:07:15,404
and doesn't want to be around me?

120
00:07:15,487 --> 00:07:18,031
I forgot to mention he's an herbivore.

121
00:07:18,115 --> 00:07:19,408
I mean, you can relate, right?

122
00:07:19,491 --> 00:07:21,535
Do you ever have the same thoughts
about Legoshi?

123
00:07:22,661 --> 00:07:25,914
{\an8}Maybe the safer choice for him
is his red deer fiancée.

124
00:07:25,998 --> 00:07:28,333
You think that could be why
he chooses her over me?

125
00:07:28,417 --> 00:07:30,043
[Haru] Well, uh, who really knows...

126
00:07:30,127 --> 00:07:31,128
I can't help it!

127
00:07:31,211 --> 00:07:33,172
There's something inside me
that can't quit him!

128
00:07:33,255 --> 00:07:34,548
He's one of a kind!

129
00:07:34,631 --> 00:07:37,718
He's got this aura,
he's always standing in the right light.

130
00:07:38,260 --> 00:07:42,014
- Oh, I could eat him up he's so cute.
- [Haru] Hm?

131
00:07:42,556 --> 00:07:46,393
Oh, uh, not like that, of course.
That's just a saying.

132
00:07:47,478 --> 00:07:49,813
Oh, I can't take it anymore!

133
00:07:49,897 --> 00:07:51,315
[crying]

134
00:07:52,441 --> 00:07:53,525
[Haru] <i>I get it.</i>

135
00:07:54,318 --> 00:07:55,360
<i>Poor Juno.</i>

136
00:07:55,444 --> 00:07:57,779
<i>She doesn't love Louis
because he's an herbivore.</i>

137
00:07:57,863 --> 00:08:01,366
<i>She just loves Louis,
who happens to be an herbivore.</i>

138
00:08:02,576 --> 00:08:04,995
<i>In the end, love is just love.</i>

139
00:08:05,871 --> 00:08:07,456
<i>That, I understand.</i>

140
00:08:07,956 --> 00:08:09,833
I know your heart.

141
00:08:09,917 --> 00:08:12,044
And I know you would never eat him.

142
00:08:12,669 --> 00:08:13,754
Well, yeah...

143
00:08:15,130 --> 00:08:16,590
[Haru] What was that?

144
00:08:16,673 --> 00:08:18,759
- Just what you said.
- [Haru] Huh?

145
00:08:19,259 --> 00:08:20,844
That's the way to say it.

146
00:08:21,345 --> 00:08:24,765
When you told me
you know I'd never eat him.

147
00:08:24,848 --> 00:08:27,518
Like you're being reassuring.

148
00:08:29,561 --> 00:08:32,231
- [shop clerk] Haru!
- [Haru] Oh, be right there!

149
00:08:33,565 --> 00:08:35,734
- Back to work.
- I appreciate it.

150
00:08:35,817 --> 00:08:37,569
Thank you for listening.

151
00:08:38,737 --> 00:08:39,571
Bye.

152
00:08:46,411 --> 00:08:47,746
All right, then.

153
00:08:48,288 --> 00:08:49,998
[heavy metal music playing]

154
00:08:51,542 --> 00:08:54,253
[tires screeching]

155
00:09:01,843 --> 00:09:05,347
Your idea of "classical" music
is a little strange.

156
00:09:05,430 --> 00:09:07,683
Well, don't you sound just like my father.

157
00:09:08,183 --> 00:09:11,520
You still don't know anything about me
do you, Louis?

158
00:09:12,062 --> 00:09:13,105
Try this on for size.

159
00:09:13,855 --> 00:09:17,317
This music makes me feel like
everything else doesn't matter.

160
00:09:18,151 --> 00:09:20,070
I know you've had a lot on your plate,

161
00:09:20,153 --> 00:09:23,198
so I appreciate you
making some time for me.

162
00:09:23,282 --> 00:09:24,825
- What'd you say?
- [music stops]

163
00:09:24,908 --> 00:09:27,452
Just that it seems
like you need a little break.

164
00:09:27,536 --> 00:09:29,121
You look tired.

165
00:09:29,204 --> 00:09:32,624
[reporter 1] <i>...as the official ambassador
for the upcoming Zoolympic bid.</i>

166
00:09:32,708 --> 00:09:33,542
[clicks]

167
00:09:35,210 --> 00:09:37,796
I would've thought
you liked all this publicity.

168
00:09:37,879 --> 00:09:39,798
I never would've guessed
you'd shy from it.

169
00:09:39,881 --> 00:09:40,924
Well, look at that.

170
00:09:41,008 --> 00:09:43,176
Seems like you don't know me
very well either.

171
00:09:43,719 --> 00:09:45,846
Doesn't seem like a problem to me.

172
00:09:45,929 --> 00:09:48,348
We have plenty of time
to get to know each other.

173
00:09:49,433 --> 00:09:50,851
[scoffs] Hmm.

174
00:10:03,155 --> 00:10:04,364
[Azuki] On a clear day,

175
00:10:04,448 --> 00:10:07,075
you can see all these
beautiful sparkles on the sea.

176
00:10:07,159 --> 00:10:09,620
- [Louis] The garden is quite lovely.
- [Azuki] That tree there...

177
00:10:09,703 --> 00:10:13,373
[chuckles] My father planted the seeds
the same day I was born.

178
00:10:14,833 --> 00:10:18,337
When we welcome our child into the world,
we should plant a tree.

179
00:10:19,588 --> 00:10:21,006
[butler] Pardon the interruption.

180
00:10:22,090 --> 00:10:23,342
[Azuki] This is from Father.

181
00:10:24,176 --> 00:10:27,054
He wanted to congratulate you
on your ambassadorship.

182
00:10:27,137 --> 00:10:28,221
It's quite an honor.

183
00:10:29,640 --> 00:10:30,974
Please enjoy.

184
00:10:31,767 --> 00:10:33,435
[chuckles softly]

185
00:10:36,146 --> 00:10:38,815
[Azuki] A toast, to my future husband.

186
00:10:44,154 --> 00:10:46,782
- I'm so proud of you.
- [Louis] Thank you.

187
00:10:46,865 --> 00:10:48,700
I have a gift for you as well.

188
00:10:50,077 --> 00:10:51,078
Blinds down.

189
00:10:56,958 --> 00:10:58,168
Because of your appointment,

190
00:10:58,251 --> 00:11:00,420
you'll be in the spotlight
quite a bit more.

191
00:11:01,088 --> 00:11:04,800
As your wife, it's only right
that I help you maintain your appearance.

192
00:11:05,592 --> 00:11:06,635
Sesame oil.

193
00:11:07,969 --> 00:11:13,308
With scents of patchouli, moss,
and bay leaf. Calming, isn't it?

194
00:11:13,392 --> 00:11:14,810
Uh... [chuckles softly]

195
00:11:20,440 --> 00:11:22,651
Uh. Hang on a minute, I'm not sure...

196
00:11:22,734 --> 00:11:24,569
Come on, don't be shy.

197
00:11:26,071 --> 00:11:26,947
[Louis] Azuki...

198
00:11:27,864 --> 00:11:31,410
[Azuki laughs] You're in good hands.

199
00:11:31,493 --> 00:11:33,495
- Try to relax.
- [Louis sighs]

200
00:11:33,578 --> 00:11:35,997
Mmm. Splendid antlers...

201
00:11:36,623 --> 00:11:39,376
[Louis] These aren't actually
my real antlers.

202
00:11:39,459 --> 00:11:42,295
They're fake, just until mine grow back.

203
00:11:42,379 --> 00:11:44,297
That doesn't matter to me.

204
00:11:44,923 --> 00:11:49,845
Whenever you're seen in public,
fake or real, these antlers are yours.

205
00:11:50,512 --> 00:11:53,682
Which means they should be
big and beautiful.

206
00:11:53,765 --> 00:11:55,142
Wouldn't you agree?

207
00:11:55,851 --> 00:11:59,062
{\an8}- Even if they're not actually my own?
- [Azuki] Yes.

208
00:11:59,146 --> 00:12:03,525
{\an8}Even if they're artificial,
they'll become real over time.

209
00:12:03,608 --> 00:12:04,985
{\an8}It just takes patience.

210
00:12:05,861 --> 00:12:07,362
{\an8}There's no guarantee of that.

211
00:12:07,446 --> 00:12:08,738
[Azuki] That's fine too.

212
00:12:09,739 --> 00:12:11,450
It's about perception.

213
00:12:11,533 --> 00:12:14,536
How you're viewed
while in the spotlight is important.

214
00:12:14,619 --> 00:12:17,247
- [Louis] Well, that's enough.
- Speaking of important,

215
00:12:17,330 --> 00:12:21,668
the city's cleanup efforts...
Seems to be on everyone's mind lately.

216
00:12:21,751 --> 00:12:22,586
What?

217
00:12:22,669 --> 00:12:24,963
If we end up winning the Zoolympic bid,

218
00:12:25,046 --> 00:12:28,717
there are pockets of the city we'd rather
not show the rest of the world.

219
00:12:28,800 --> 00:12:29,885
I guess...

220
00:12:29,968 --> 00:12:32,804
Certain elements
will need to be cleaned up.

221
00:12:32,888 --> 00:12:35,140
For example, the Carnivore District.

222
00:12:35,223 --> 00:12:36,057
Wha--

223
00:12:37,684 --> 00:12:39,436
The Black Market, is that what you mean?

224
00:12:39,519 --> 00:12:43,356
I heard about some unsavory elements
fighting over something around there.

225
00:12:43,440 --> 00:12:46,735
So Father was saying that
they're going to clean it all up.

226
00:12:46,818 --> 00:12:49,404
This is the first I've heard
of something like that.

227
00:12:49,488 --> 00:12:52,282
What a shame. I'm looking forward to it.

228
00:12:55,452 --> 00:12:57,078
[Louis] I should get going soon.

229
00:12:57,621 --> 00:13:01,041
[Azuki] Are you sure?
The sea is beautiful at sunrise.

230
00:13:01,917 --> 00:13:03,668
{\an8}You want to watch it with me?

231
00:13:06,254 --> 00:13:07,172
MADARA-GUMI

232
00:13:07,255 --> 00:13:09,299
[Miso] Out of the way! Move it!

233
00:13:10,217 --> 00:13:12,469
Madara-Gumi coming through!

234
00:13:12,552 --> 00:13:15,388
[man 1] It's the Madara-Gumi!
Clear the way, clear out!

235
00:13:15,472 --> 00:13:17,224
- [man 2] Oh, crap, run!
- [man 3] Not again.

236
00:13:17,307 --> 00:13:18,892
[woman] Oh, my goodness!
Go back home.

237
00:13:18,975 --> 00:13:19,893
[growls]

238
00:13:19,976 --> 00:13:22,562
Hey, old man. How's business?

239
00:13:22,646 --> 00:13:25,774
Good, thank you.
Here you are, this month's tribute.

240
00:13:25,857 --> 00:13:27,234
[Miso] Ooh. [laughs]

241
00:13:27,734 --> 00:13:30,737
Yeah, very nice. You're in good hands.

242
00:13:30,820 --> 00:13:34,241
We'll keep an eye on your shop here
and make sure it's safe. [laughs]

243
00:13:34,324 --> 00:13:35,617
Aah! [groans]

244
00:13:35,700 --> 00:13:38,036
What the hell is this? Move it!

245
00:13:38,119 --> 00:13:39,120
[man 4] The hell are you doing?

246
00:13:39,204 --> 00:13:41,248
[Ten] If your uncultured brain
can handle it,

247
00:13:41,331 --> 00:13:43,291
- I have a free life lesson.
- [Miso] Shut it!

248
00:13:43,375 --> 00:13:47,087
Fine stilettos like these
are made for walking the red carpet.

249
00:13:47,170 --> 00:13:48,046
[Miso] Cut the crap!

250
00:13:48,129 --> 00:13:51,800
[Ten] If you don't watch yourself,
I'll soak a carpet red with your blood.

251
00:13:51,883 --> 00:13:52,759
[Miso] Is that so?

252
00:13:52,842 --> 00:13:56,012
You're getting pretty cocky there,
aren't you, Ten?

253
00:13:56,096 --> 00:13:58,056
[laughs] Can you blame me?

254
00:13:58,557 --> 00:14:00,850
You're looking at what
the Black Market needs right now.

255
00:14:00,934 --> 00:14:03,853
- A helping hand. The Inari-Gumi.
- [woman 1] You know that's right.

256
00:14:03,937 --> 00:14:06,815
The streets will always belong
to the Madara-Gumi.

257
00:14:06,898 --> 00:14:09,359
- Right!
- Get this tacky junk out of here.

258
00:14:09,442 --> 00:14:12,153
With pleasure, if you can take me down.

259
00:14:12,654 --> 00:14:15,699
Ha! Little girl, big words.

260
00:14:17,367 --> 00:14:19,244
- [woman] Watch out!
- [grunts]

261
00:14:20,662 --> 00:14:21,913
Looks like it's playtime.

262
00:14:26,459 --> 00:14:28,545
And I just paid this stand off.

263
00:14:29,087 --> 00:14:31,506
[man] Jeez, do we have to do this
every day?

264
00:14:31,590 --> 00:14:34,968
[man 2] I miss the days when Shishi-Gumi
had that deer for a boss.

265
00:14:37,637 --> 00:14:38,680
What?

266
00:14:38,763 --> 00:14:41,683
{\an8}That's unreal. Who has the money for that?

267
00:14:46,104 --> 00:14:47,480
- [Jimma grunts]
- [thwacking]

268
00:14:47,564 --> 00:14:48,607
You bastard!

269
00:14:48,690 --> 00:14:50,567
[Free] You know not to screw with us!

270
00:14:51,109 --> 00:14:52,944
Everybody gets protection,

271
00:14:53,028 --> 00:14:54,988
- 'cause everybody always pays!
- [Jimma] Pay up!

272
00:14:56,615 --> 00:14:57,824
{\an8}Where's that "protection"

273
00:14:57,908 --> 00:15:01,077
{\an8}when the Inari-Gumi or the Madara-Gumi
destroy my shop?

274
00:15:01,161 --> 00:15:02,329
{\an8}Then I'd have no problem.

275
00:15:02,871 --> 00:15:04,789
{\an8}[Victor] You've got a dirty mouth.

276
00:15:04,873 --> 00:15:05,707
{\an8}[turtle groans]

277
00:15:06,541 --> 00:15:08,043
{\an8}You know it's the truth!

278
00:15:08,126 --> 00:15:11,588
{\an8}I'm still waiting till
we get any kind of real protection.

279
00:15:12,422 --> 00:15:13,465
What?

280
00:15:13,548 --> 00:15:16,885
Come on, we never even sat down
and signed a contract.

281
00:15:16,968 --> 00:15:19,304
You guys are just holed up
in your hideout,

282
00:15:19,387 --> 00:15:22,098
{\an8}abandoned by the deer
and by your mixed boss too.

283
00:15:22,182 --> 00:15:23,600
{\an8}Gotta say, it's pretty embarrassing.

284
00:15:23,683 --> 00:15:26,686
{\an8}So, what you're sayin' is,
you'd like trip to the bottom of the sea?

285
00:15:26,770 --> 00:15:27,604
{\an8}Oh.

286
00:15:27,687 --> 00:15:30,482
{\an8}- All right. Okay, I'll pay.
- Huh?

287
00:15:30,565 --> 00:15:33,860
{\an8}You win! I'll pay up. I'll give you extra!

288
00:15:33,944 --> 00:15:35,779
Mercy! Please show mercy!

289
00:15:35,862 --> 00:15:37,614
[laughs]

290
00:15:37,697 --> 00:15:40,909
Now you're talking.
That's what I like to hear.

291
00:15:40,992 --> 00:15:42,577
- [footsteps approaching]
- Huh?

292
00:15:44,871 --> 00:15:45,747
[gasps]

293
00:15:46,414 --> 00:15:47,749
What the hell?

294
00:15:52,712 --> 00:15:54,839
[sighs] I'm exhausted.

295
00:15:55,882 --> 00:15:58,218
As a lone herbivore
walking through the Black Market,

296
00:15:58,301 --> 00:16:00,845
I thought it would be safer
if I had a price tag.

297
00:16:00,929 --> 00:16:03,515
- But it just made me stand out more.
- No surprise there.

298
00:16:03,598 --> 00:16:06,393
[Jimma] As usual, you're totally fierce.

299
00:16:06,935 --> 00:16:08,812
- [Free] So then...
- [Louis] Hm?

300
00:16:08,895 --> 00:16:11,940
Uh... So does your stunt in the Black Market

301
00:16:12,023 --> 00:16:14,818
mean that you're returning
to lead the Shishi-Gumi?

302
00:16:14,901 --> 00:16:16,403
[all exclaim]

303
00:16:17,862 --> 00:16:20,323
No. You know I can't do that.
I turned that down.

304
00:16:20,407 --> 00:16:22,075
- [all sigh wearily]
- [Victor] What're you doin' to us?

305
00:16:22,158 --> 00:16:23,660
- [Miguel] Getting our hopes up!
- [Victor sighs]

306
00:16:23,743 --> 00:16:26,037
I've got some news you need to hear.

307
00:16:26,121 --> 00:16:27,956
I wanted to make sure
you got the heads-up.

308
00:16:28,039 --> 00:16:30,583
The city is going to start
cleaning up the Black Market.

309
00:16:30,667 --> 00:16:32,293
"Cleaning up"?

310
00:16:32,377 --> 00:16:34,796
I don't know specifically
how it's going to work,

311
00:16:34,879 --> 00:16:37,590
but I figured it was something important
you needed to know.

312
00:16:37,674 --> 00:16:41,344
You came all the way here
just to tell us this?

313
00:16:41,845 --> 00:16:43,972
Uh, yeah.

314
00:16:44,889 --> 00:16:47,350
And now that I have, see ya.

315
00:16:47,434 --> 00:16:50,145
- [Jimma] Uh, hang on, where's the fire?
- [Free] Hold on a minute!

316
00:16:50,228 --> 00:16:53,773
You're already here,
might as well hang a bit.

317
00:16:53,857 --> 00:16:56,276
I bet you're starving! Right?

318
00:16:56,860 --> 00:16:58,278
We'll make something nice!

319
00:16:59,404 --> 00:17:01,322
[sniffing]

320
00:17:01,406 --> 00:17:04,951
You know,
you've got kind of a different smell.

321
00:17:05,035 --> 00:17:08,121
- [Dolph] Yeah, I thought the same thing.
- [sighs]

322
00:17:08,204 --> 00:17:09,831
I've been through a lot lately.

323
00:17:09,914 --> 00:17:13,418
- [Agata] I bet it's about a woman.
- Aw, guys. Come on.

324
00:17:14,044 --> 00:17:16,796
{\an8}You guys have to know
that you really stink.

325
00:17:17,338 --> 00:17:18,715
{\an8}You're bathing, right?

326
00:17:18,798 --> 00:17:22,218
We do get wet from all the tears
from the broken hearts,

327
00:17:22,302 --> 00:17:24,179
- but never under a shower.
- Hey!

328
00:17:24,262 --> 00:17:26,431
- [all laughing]
- Come on, stop it.

329
00:17:26,514 --> 00:17:28,516
You think I wanna be a stinky lion
like you guys?

330
00:17:28,600 --> 00:17:30,101
<i>What's wrong with me?</i>

331
00:17:30,185 --> 00:17:33,855
<i>I can't believe the smell of this pride
is actually comforting.</i>

332
00:17:33,938 --> 00:17:35,690
[Victor] Come on, he came all this way,

333
00:17:35,774 --> 00:17:38,610
and we don't have a single thing
we can make for Louis?

334
00:17:38,693 --> 00:17:41,362
Eh, it's not like we even know
what "gourmet" means.

335
00:17:41,446 --> 00:17:42,947
Well, we have this meat!

336
00:17:43,031 --> 00:17:46,493
Idiot!
Find something for herbivores.

337
00:17:46,993 --> 00:17:47,827
Oh!

338
00:17:48,870 --> 00:17:50,121
[Miguel] What do you got?

339
00:17:53,541 --> 00:17:55,251
[all] This is it!

340
00:17:56,169 --> 00:17:57,170
Ta-da!

341
00:17:57,253 --> 00:17:58,713
Apologies for the delay!

342
00:17:58,797 --> 00:18:00,799
We present, the finest,
most premium melon,

343
00:18:00,882 --> 00:18:03,051
prepared just for our friend Louis!

344
00:18:03,134 --> 00:18:05,386
- [Agata shushing]
- Huh?

345
00:18:05,470 --> 00:18:06,638
[shushes]

346
00:18:07,138 --> 00:18:08,973
- [Victor] Hm?
- [Jimma] What?

347
00:18:14,104 --> 00:18:15,438
Unbelievable...

348
00:18:16,272 --> 00:18:20,401
We've got an herbivore layin' here
in a carnivore den.

349
00:18:21,152 --> 00:18:23,029
And he's out like a light.

350
00:18:25,907 --> 00:18:28,409
{\an8}UDON BEBEBE

351
00:18:33,456 --> 00:18:35,166
[guard] Oh, looks great!

352
00:18:35,250 --> 00:18:36,835
[Legoshi sighs] Please enjoy.

353
00:18:40,046 --> 00:18:41,131
<i>Where's Haru?</i>

354
00:18:41,798 --> 00:18:44,884
<i>I remember her saying
she was gonna be working today.</i>

355
00:18:45,677 --> 00:18:46,678
[sniff] Oh?

356
00:18:46,761 --> 00:18:48,471
[sniffs] <i>Haru's scent!</i>

357
00:18:55,645 --> 00:18:58,898
<i>Uh, the smell is coming from here, but...</i>

358
00:19:00,358 --> 00:19:01,943
<i>guess she's not here after all.</i>

359
00:19:02,485 --> 00:19:06,197
Huh? [sniffing]

360
00:19:06,281 --> 00:19:07,448
<i>That smell...</i>

361
00:19:08,533 --> 00:19:10,785
<i>No way. It can't be.</i>

362
00:19:10,869 --> 00:19:14,873
[sniffing]

363
00:19:15,540 --> 00:19:16,916
<i>Melon!</i>

364
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:19,043
[student 1] You see that?
Seems kind of shady...

365
00:19:19,127 --> 00:19:20,003
Huh?

366
00:19:20,086 --> 00:19:21,504
- [student 2] Should we report him?
<i>- Oh, no...</i>

367
00:19:23,423 --> 00:19:26,426
- [Dom] Wait. Isn't that Legoshi?
- [Legoshi] Huh?

368
00:19:27,218 --> 00:19:29,804
Hey! What's up, Dom?

369
00:19:29,888 --> 00:19:30,889
[laughs]

370
00:19:31,598 --> 00:19:33,683
It's fine. I know him from school.

371
00:19:33,766 --> 00:19:34,601
- Ah.
- Oh.

372
00:19:36,144 --> 00:19:38,396
Well, hi! I didn't know you went here.

373
00:19:38,479 --> 00:19:40,148
Yeah, I'm studying art.

374
00:19:40,732 --> 00:19:44,319
Can't believe I ran into you.
This is a nice surprise!

375
00:19:47,697 --> 00:19:50,575
[Dom] Do you still keep in touch
with everyone from the drama club?

376
00:19:50,658 --> 00:19:53,161
[Legoshi] Well,
I did drop by the club last month.

377
00:19:53,244 --> 00:19:54,621
Everyone was hard at work.

378
00:19:54,704 --> 00:19:59,542
You know, it's tough at the school,
separating carnivores and herbivores.

379
00:19:59,626 --> 00:20:01,878
It's the same even for clubs, I hear.

380
00:20:01,961 --> 00:20:04,172
So, have you been
in touch with them at all?

381
00:20:04,255 --> 00:20:07,175
Well, I do chat with Kai every now
and then, I suppose.

382
00:20:07,258 --> 00:20:09,677
- Kai, huh? Is he doin' all right?
- [laughs]

383
00:20:10,511 --> 00:20:12,472
He said he thrives in adversity.

384
00:20:12,555 --> 00:20:15,516
Seems like he's embraced becoming
a real part of the drama club

385
00:20:15,600 --> 00:20:16,893
instead of just an "actor."

386
00:20:16,976 --> 00:20:18,770
[Legoshi laughs]
Good on him!

387
00:20:18,853 --> 00:20:22,023
Out there on the lawn,
what were you sniffing around for?

388
00:20:22,106 --> 00:20:22,982
Huh?

389
00:20:23,066 --> 00:20:24,943
Oh, uh... [chuckles nervously]

390
00:20:25,026 --> 00:20:26,194
You don't have to say.

391
00:20:26,277 --> 00:20:28,947
Oh, uh... Just taking in the scents.

392
00:20:29,030 --> 00:20:32,242
Right now,
that's not the best look on campus.

393
00:20:32,325 --> 00:20:35,203
There's been a lot unusual things
going on lately.

394
00:20:35,828 --> 00:20:37,080
What do you mean by that?

395
00:20:37,705 --> 00:20:38,915
[Dom exhales]

396
00:20:38,998 --> 00:20:41,209
Like a professor falling to their death.

397
00:20:41,793 --> 00:20:44,879
Or a student almost getting devoured.

398
00:20:44,963 --> 00:20:47,090
Everyone's a bit on edge right now.

399
00:20:47,882 --> 00:20:49,842
Wow, that sounds like a lot.

400
00:20:49,926 --> 00:20:51,010
[Dom] It's not just here,

401
00:20:51,094 --> 00:20:54,472
but it seems everywhere
is getting dangerous, don't ya think?

402
00:20:54,555 --> 00:20:55,723
[Legoshi] Mm-hm.

403
00:20:55,807 --> 00:20:57,517
You going to the Festival?

404
00:20:57,600 --> 00:21:00,645
- [Legoshi] That's the plan.
- Cool, hope to see you there.

405
00:21:00,728 --> 00:21:02,522
[Legoshi] Yeah. Take care!

406
00:21:04,107 --> 00:21:05,066
[sighs]

407
00:21:06,693 --> 00:21:08,361
[long sniff]

408
00:21:11,322 --> 00:21:14,200
<i>Here's the scent I picked up
when I showed up on campus.</i>

409
00:21:15,243 --> 00:21:16,703
So about Melon,

410
00:21:16,786 --> 00:21:20,373
apparently he's called "Professor"
in polite society.

411
00:21:26,462 --> 00:21:27,547
[Legoshi] <i>This is it.</i>

412
00:21:34,012 --> 00:21:35,513
[exhales] Hmm.

413
00:21:39,517 --> 00:21:40,852
<i>Melon...</i>

414
00:21:41,811 --> 00:21:44,022
<i>You're not getting away.</i>

415
00:21:44,856 --> 00:21:47,275
{\an8}We're told that early this morning,
in this apartment right behind me...

416
00:21:47,358 --> 00:21:49,319
{\an8}BREAKING NEWS: BROWN BEAR SUSPECTED
IN DEVOURING INCIDENT ALSO FOUND MURDERED

417
00:21:49,402 --> 00:21:51,029
{\an8}...a female llama was devoured.

418
00:21:51,112 --> 00:21:53,448
The brown bear
believed to have committed the crime

419
00:21:53,531 --> 00:21:55,575
was also found dead at the scene.

420
00:21:56,075 --> 00:21:58,745
This quiet street connecting
the Algama District and Center Street

421
00:21:58,828 --> 00:22:00,913
is where we find our gruesome scene.

422
00:22:00,997 --> 00:22:02,999
[closing theme song playing]
